th1-surjection-curation-001+math1-bijection-curation-001+math1-union-curation-001+math1-proper-curation-001+math1-complement-curation-001+math1-complement-render-001+math1-division-curation-001+math1-reciprocal-curation-001+math1-inequality-curation-001+math1-inequality-feedback-001+math1-maximum-curation-001+math1-minimum-curation-001+math1-boundedset-curation-001+math1-endpoint-curation-001+audit-groups-20261027+topup-math-i-20261028+topup-math-ii-20261028+topup-pt-20261028+topup-math-iii-20261028+v3-2026-11-02+v3-2026-11-10+v3-2026-11-10+v3-2026-11-10+v3-2026-11-10+type-mix-retire-20261112+type-mix-topup-20261112+type-mix-retire2-20261112+fill-20261112+fill2-20261112","concept_id":"Year-1/1b-Programming-for-EOR/vectorized-operations.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/1b-Programming-for-EOR/vectorized-operations.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In R, what does it mean that an operation such as `+` or `sqrt()` is vectorized?","options":["It reduces a whole vector to one summary number, such as its total.","It has to be written once for each element, one command per position.","It works on vectors only after they have been turned into matrices.","It acts on a whole vector in one call, element by element, one result per element."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ff32ec320c342f7b46e4bfe5","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For `x <- c(4, 9, 36)`, which statement about the call `sqrt(x)` is correct?","options":["It returns the single number 7, the square root of the sum of `x`.","It returns the vector `2 3 6` and leaves `x` unchanged.","It changes `x` itself to `2 3 6` and prints nothing.","It works only element by element in separate calls, such as `sqrt(x[1])`."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bf2f4cce188660cc3123c359","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does `c(1, 2, 3) + c(10, 20, 30)` return?","options":["`[1] 11 22 33`","`[1] 66`","`[1]  1  2  3 10 20 30`","`[1] 11 21 31`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"01e416c91ed71ff355087f53","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does `2^c(0, 1, 3)` return?","options":["`[1] 0 1 9`","`[1] 0 2 6`","`[1] 1 2 8`","`[1] 16`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4f1a187974af79faee50a8e2","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does `sqrt(c(4, -9, 16))` return?","options":["`[1] 2 3 4`, without any warning","`[1]   2 NaN   4`, with the warning `NaNs produced`","the error `NaNs produced`, with no result at all","`[1] NaN`, with the warning `NaNs produced`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f4d820fb40e782e3f5b16224","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"In linear algebra, $2\\boldsymbol{x}-\\boldsymbol{y}$ is formed for $\\boldsymbol{x}=(1,0,2)$ and $\\boldsymbol{y}=(3,1,-1)$. With `x <- c(1, 0, 2); y <- c(3, 1, -1)`, what does `2 * x - y` return?","options":["`[1] -1 -1  5`","`[1] 3`","`[1] -1 -1  3`","`[1] -2 -1  3 -2 -1  3`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ace4d9bda764dd20685344c0","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A vector of marks `m <- c(10, 20, 30)` is rescaled with `m / 10 + 1`. What does R return?","options":["`[1] 7`","`[1] 1 2 3 1`","`[1] 2 3 4`","`[1]  2 20 30`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"46204662b521d91b1263a828","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does `exp(c(0, 1))` return?","options":["`[1] 0.000000 2.718282`","`[1] 3.718282`","`[1] 2.718282 7.389056`","`[1] 1.000000 2.718282`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"85db49755eff181f4d87e65e","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Three products cost `price <- c(3, 8, 2)` and are bought in quantities `qty <- c(4, 1, 5)`, in the same product order. What does `sum(price * qty)` return?","options":["`[1] 130`","`[1] 30`","`[1] 12  8 10`","`[1] 23`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"04820d65e4eaf62ef101174d","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"`price` lists the prices of three products in the order A, B, C, but `qty` lists their quantities in the order B, C, A. What does `price * qty` give?","options":["The correct amounts, as R matches the products automatically when both vectors have length 3.","A warning that the two vectors are in different orders, followed by the products.","Products of the values at equal positions, which are wrong here, with no message at all.","An error, because the two vectors list the products in different orders."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a58fe2a5aa4c4d0eb1d35b5e","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For two numeric vectors `x` and `y` of length $n$, how does `x * y` relate to operations from linear algebra?","options":["It is the vector of products $x_i y_i$; the inner product is `sum(x * y)`.","It is the inner product $\\sum_i x_i y_i$, a single number.","It is the $n\\times n$ matrix with entries $x_i y_j$.","It is scalar multiplication, with `y` acting as the scalar."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7cd14ae885147ea25565a21c","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What does `round(sqrt(c(2, 9, 20)), 1)` return?","options":["`[1] 1.414214 3.000000 4.472136`","`[1] 5.6`","`[1] 8.9`","`[1] 1.4 3.0 4.5`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d162f0d262a2e95e3bb34eed","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(3, 4, 12)`, what does `sqrt(sum(x^2))`, the length of `x` as a vector in linear algebra, return?","options":["`[1] 19`","`[1] 13`","`[1]  3  4 12`","`[1] 4.358899`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"aba4de6995fb35307bbeac56","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What does `log(c(1, 10, 100), base = 10)` return?","options":["`[1] 0 1 2`","`[1] 0.000000 2.302585 4.605170`","`[1] 2.045323`","`[1] 3`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7380bbb9566019aefa0aa175","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What does `x <- c(4, 6, 11); x - mean(x)` return?","options":["`[1]  3  1 -4`","`[1] 0`","`[1] -3 -1  4`","`[1] -3`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"04440d35fdac75c448840180","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For two $2\\times2$ matrices `A` and `B` in R, what does `A * B` compute?","options":["The matrix product $AB$ from linear algebra.","The single number $\\sum_{i,j} a_{ij} b_{ij}$ over all four entries.","An error, because `*` works only for vectors, not for matrices.","The $2\\times2$ matrix with entries $a_{ij} b_{ij}$, position by position."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5181f4701e16f6ed0642f5cd","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Sales in three years are `x <- c(100, 110, 99)`. What does `x[-1] / x[-length(x)]`, the ratio of each year to the year before, return?","options":["`[1] 1.1 0.9`","`[1] 0.9090909 1.1111111`","`[1] 1.00 1.10 0.99`","`[1] 0.99`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9433f8700c9fda0d6cfc1ec2","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_vectorized_operations_4aaf00af_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Prices per item are `price <- c(1.5, 3, 4)` for milk, eggs and tea. The quantities were typed as `qty <- c(2, 6, 1)` in the order tea, milk, eggs. Which expression gives the correct bill?","options":["`sum(price * qty)`","`sum(price * qty[c(3, 1, 2)])`","`sum(price * qty[c(2, 3, 1)])`","`sum(price) * sum(qty)`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1ebed7c5e5eeff143eeb6d60","time_limit":40}]}}